BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>ORO - Saturn's rings</h1>
<p>The judging rig for ORO's planetary rings (2026-09-12): a DeltaGlider in a circular
orbit just outside the A ring, inclined 25 degrees, near Saturn's northern summer
solstice so the ring's shadow lies as a broad band across the globe. One orbit carries
you over the lit face, through the ring plane, and under the backlit face.</p>
<p>ORO panel: WORLD -&gt; RINGS. The pill is the A/B - off is stock exactly. Watch: the
sheet going opaque near edge-on, the backlit inversion (the B ring dark, the Cassini
Division bright), the shadow band on the planet with the Division as a bright line
inside it, and the ship dimming as it crosses the shadow.</p>
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 57897.25
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship GL-01
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET GL-01
  MODE Extern
  POS 6.50 -35.0 20.0
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_HUD
  TYPE Orbit
END_HUD

BEGIN_MFD Left
  TYPE Orbit
  REF Saturn
END_MFD

BEGIN_MFD Right
  TYPE Map
  REF Saturn
END_MFD

BEGIN_SHIPS
GL-01:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting Saturn
  ELEMENTS 151403000.0 0.0005 25.0 40.0 0.0 0.0 57897.25
  AROT 0.0 0.0 0.0
  PRPLEVEL 0:1.000 1:1.000
  NAVFREQ 0 0 0 0
  GEAR 0 0.0000
  AAP 0:0 0:0 0:0
END
END_SHIPS
